BanMido wrote:
>
> Anyway, it is my observation that, as soon as I enter the temple, the
> level goes bonkers and a seemingly unending stream of monsters
> appears. I think the effect is particularly pronounced, if the temple
> is co-aligned. I simply cannot get out of the sanctuary or else I am
> slaughtered by hard and multiple hitting monsters like ants, orcs,
> centaurs, elves zapping wands left, right and center ... you know, the
> works.

I make a point of clearly out the level of hostiles before spending any
time in the shrine.  I check the alignment and move on to clear the
level, especially if it's cross aligned and I won't get benefit then
from a sacri-fest.

> Is this what usually happens or am I doing something wrong? How do I
> deal with that? Sometimes a peaceful dwarf simply brings down all the
> walls of the temple and the temple itself gets flooded with nasties
> and I get no protection whatsoever from ranged attacks.

Because of the digging I clear the mine town of peaceful monsters
other than the watch, and I try to get my pet enough combat experience
to take out the regular watchmen on the way down and the watch
captain on the way up.  I loose a lot of pets doing that.

> Now as I typed about the bones file, I am thinking could that be the
> source of problem? Should I clear all bones files and see what
> happens?

Or work through clearing the level of hostiles.  Bones files are finite,
especially if you encounter one and then die on a different level.  The
number of monsters in any one bones level is finite, and the number of
bones files is finite.


